kosha rated-torque

  -- the maximum continuous torque a motor / actuator can deliver at a joint
  -- a physical limit of the stepper or servo motor
  --
  -- in the chala-apeksha model:
  --   rated-torque is the limit on τ[i] in the joint's own frame
  --   the actual required torque at joint i depends on:
  --     - the link's moment of inertia (I[i])
  --     - the angular acceleration (α[i])
  --     - the chala-apeksha coupling terms from all other joints
  --     - gravitational load (m·g·r·cos(θ_world))
  --   if required-torque > rated-torque → motor cannot execute the motion plan
  --
  -- motor-check tantra compares required torque against rated-torque
  -- margin-torque = rated-torque - required-torque
  --   margin > 0 → feasible
  --   margin < 0 → infeasible — must reduce speed or redesign

  "subanta-swarupa"
  "domain-robotics-sthita kinematic-chain-yukta"
  "torque-abheda"
  "joint-yukta"
  "newton-metre-matra"
  "seema-sthita"
  "chala-apeksha-sthita"

shabda rated-torque, max-torque, torque-rating / the-maximum-torque-the-motor-at-a-joint-can-deliver

